# Services

## Rules

- Inject models with `@InjectModel`; use real CRUD — no placeholder strings
- Throw Nest exceptions with `ApiMessage` (and field `errors` on conflicts)
- Ids are strings: `findById(id)`, never `findById(+id)`
- Hash passwords with `bcrypt` cost `10` before save
- Secrets on schema: `select: false`; use `.select('+password')` when needed
- Let `AllExceptionsFilter` map Mongoose errors — don’t swallow them

```typescript
throw new NotFoundException(ApiMessage.USER_NOT_FOUND);
throw new ConflictException({
  message: ApiMessage.USER_ALREADY_EXISTS,
  errors: { email: 'Email is already taken' },
});
```

## Avoid

```typescript
return 'This action updates a #${id} category';
throw new Error('fail');
```
